      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. For the lesson though, I want to make sure I'm being accurate about the legal theory. Some people argue that substantive due process is actually a problematic way to interpret the law because it lets judges basically make up new rights that aren't in the text. How would you address that critique in my lesson plan?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
